84  eventually takes him across the world to  egypt to visit amir saad bin arbidos the  presence of this oil barren character  kicks off a deluge of astonishingly  tone-deaf stereotypes about people  hailing from the middle east and north  africa every scene set in egypt and  wonder woman 1984 even ones in which  arbidose is off screen are jaw-dropping  in their regressive portrayals of mena  individuals naturally such depictions  were bound to generate controversy as  well as a few thoughtful essays breaking  down how these scenes were so off the  mark one of the more insightful examples  of these breakdowns came in a piece for  slate where writer roxanna hadidi broke  down some of the worst cultural  misconceptions in wonder woman 1984.  these include characters referring to  arbidose as your highness despite egypt  being a democracy in the 1980s as well  as the ways in which arbidose's costume  resembles traditional attire from saudi  arabia or the united arab emirates  rather than egypt such inaccuracies feed  into dehumanizing stereotypes of mena  individuals it appears that wonder woman  1984 a film that seeks to celebrate the  cinema of the 1980s was unable to escape  the racial caricatures that was so  rampant in that era there are countless  things audiences could have been  expecting to see in wonder woman 1984  but surely nobody was expecting a  weirdly dismissive approach to sexual  assault this shocking development  emerged in a scene in which diana prince  discovers that her wish on the wishing  rock has come true steve trevor has come  back to life rather than just having  trevor resurrected in his original body  though the film has trevor inhabit the  body of a total stranger with trevor  back from the dead he and prince proceed  to have sex which should be a passionate  romantic reunion takes on all kinds of  unsettling tones however given that it  involves a sexual partner who cannot and  did not consent to be involved wonder  woman 1984 never addresses these  disturbing implications and simply plows  ahead on its story about wishes getting  more and more out of control  understandably this storytelling detour  inspired an outcry when the movie was  released tragically reflecting how even  modern blockbusters can fall prey to  problematic tropes  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

